ioctl - inspect or control a terminal descriptor

SYNOPSIS
    #include "ioctl.h"
    int ioctl(int fd, int request, void *data);

DESCRIPTION
    The descriptor must refer to the system console. TIOCGETA and
    TIOCSETA, TIOCSETAW, or TIOCSETAF take a pointer to struct termios.
    See termios(2) for the corresponding library functions.

    TIOCGWINSZ reads, and TIOCSWINSZ sets, the console viewport size.
    Both take a pointer to struct winsize. The ws_row and ws_col
    members hold rows and columns. The pixel fields read as zero.
    Changes require a foreground caller and dimensions of at least
    two rows and columns, within the display limits.

RETURN VALUES
    Zero on success, or -1 for an invalid descriptor, request,
    argument, dimension, or caller.

SEE ALSO
    man(1), stty(1), termios(2), ttyctl(2)
